# One test finds that a typed array has a fixed length and that a position lies inside it. Behind it a read is the load of the vector and the load of the element, and a store the same with a store:
# no test of the mode, no arm that looks the position up by value or calls the run time, so a function that only tests and accesses has no frame. The read finds an element, so its type has no `undefined` and its result is unboxed.
# Each kind of view with element accesses in line has such code, for integer and double positions and stored values, in the three code shapes. Beside them stand the accesses without the test, and the one store that takes the operation whatever is known
# FORM: Placed
# OPTIONS: heat=OnlyLoopsAreHot check=validate-back-end
# RUN: generate-code calls
# RUN(S): code-shapes
# RUN(R): pass ChooseRepresentations

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
function f0 name="readOfInt8Array" parameters=[{type=Int8Array}, {type=i32}] results=[{type=anything}] {
    v2 = IsInsideView v0, v1 typedArrayType=1
    TestAndBranch v2 -> taken b1(| 0), notTaken b2()
  b1(v3):
    v4 = GetTypedArrayElement v0, v1, v3 typedArrayType=1 level=Proven [isInsideView]
    Return v4
  b2():
    v5 = Undefined
    Return v5
}
